1. Domain Controller

The Windows Server virtual machine acts as the Domain Controller.

Responsibilities include:

Active Directory authentication
User account management
Computer account management
DNS service
Domain management
Centralized access management
2. Windows 11 Client

The Windows 11 virtual machine acts as the end-user workstation.

The client is used to:

Connect to the domain
Resolve the domain through DNS
Join the Active Directory domain
Authenticate using domain credentials
Test domain connectivity
Simulate common end-user support scenarios
