🌐 Active Directory Domain

A dedicated Active Directory domain was created for the lab.

Example:

ad.domain.com

The domain is hosted by the Windows Server Domain Controller.

The Domain Controller provides centralized authentication and directory services to domain-joined client computers.

Note: The domain name above represents the lab environment and is not intended for production use.

⚙️ Phase 1 — Windows Server Setup

The first step was creating a Windows Server virtual machine using Oracle VirtualBox.

The server was configured with appropriate:

CPU resources
RAM
Virtual hard disk
Network adapter
Windows Server installation

After installation, the server was prepared for Active Directory deployment.

🌐 Phase 2 — Network Configuration

A stable network configuration is important for Active Directory.

The Domain Controller was configured with a suitable IP configuration.

Example:

IP Address:      192.168.x.x
Subnet Mask:     255.255.255.0
Default Gateway: 192.168.x.x
Preferred DNS:   Domain Controller IP

The exact addresses depend on the VirtualBox network configuration.

🧩 Phase 3 — Installing Active Directory Domain Services

Active Directory Domain Services was installed on the Windows Server.

AD DS provides centralized management of:

Users
Computers
Groups
Authentication
Domain resources
Security policies

After installing the AD DS role, the server was promoted to a Domain Controller.

🏢 Phase 4 — Domain Controller Promotion

The Windows Server was promoted to a Domain Controller and configured with the lab Active Directory domain.

Example:

ad.domain.com

After the promotion process, the server became responsible for providing domain authentication and directory services.

